(story title) Forensic Necromancy: A Murder in Nineveh
(story author) Daniel M. Stelzer
(story ifid) 185CEA3F-ED51-498B-92D7-C1A62F2D431C
(story noun) A Historical Mystery
(story release 0)
(story blurb)
	The theory holds up, and the lab data is promising. But if you want to be the first PhD in Forensic Necromancy, you need results the world can’t ignore. Which is why you’re now creeping through Nineveh in the dead of night, searching for human remains in situ. What millennia-old secrets are waiting to be unearthed? And most importantly—will they be enough to impress a thesis committee?

